en says the world  needs a new type of hero  we need new heroes  one suited for the times we're in carly  concludes saying the shield should be  destroyed as it's a reminder of a bygone  era  john and lamar have tracked down sam and  bucky who are with the fugitive zemo  they want to bring zemo in but he's the  only one who knows where donya's funeral  is being held sam wants to go in alone  thinking that carly in this vulnerable  state of losing a loved one will be more  willing to talk and for the most  part he is right at its core sam and  carly are fighting for the same thing  she even says the people i'm fighting  are trying to take your home  some a reference to the bank trying to  take his and his sister's fishing boat  but the ways the two of them go about  bringing  justice are wildly different carly will  do whatever it takes even killing the  innocent while sam won't stoop to that  level  and just as sam starts to earn carly's  trust the new cap has to stroll in  and screw everything up zemo manages to  escape from his handcuffs and also  somehow acquire a gun  a gun which he'll later use to shoot  carly this seems to be a common  occurrence with him  back in episode 2 we saw how matthias  was shot in the stomach by cat but later  is somehow healed this seems to be the  case with carly in this episode the  serum having advanced  regenerative qualities in episode 3 we  learned from nagel the creator of the  serum that 20 vials were made  here at the cemetery we see seven of  them and here on the ground we see eight  plus there were the vials carly and her  team took this is all to say that when  zemo smashes the files the show hints  that there is only one left and that one  captain america will use on himself  however the show playing fast and loose  with these numbers you never  know when another one could be at play  carly gets a text from the power broker  funny it's always a text  and never a call whoever is on the other  end is wanting his or her identity  hidden with the power broker sam and  bucky and cal and lamar on her tail she  decides to separate them  and pick off captain america with their  eight hours up  io and two of her dora melanche nombel  and yama comfort zemo cap and lamar  arrive and a fight ensues with zemo  making an el chapo escape a nod to how  mexican drug lord  el chapo guzman escaped his prison via  hidden passageway under his cell's  washroom bucky is  literally disarmed something he didn't  know could happen which leads me to  believe this might happen again in the  future  cap however gets the worst of it getting  his ass beaten so hard he says  thank you sir i have another oh not that  one they weren't even super soldier  and this has all been part of how the  writers have been building up his  character so he'd get to the point where  we'd believe he'd take this super  soldier serum  this started all the way back in episode  2 when he talks about the pressure of  being the new cap  and living up to expectations everybody  in the world expects me to be  something and i don't want to fail them  in a one-on-one with his bff cap asked  lamar if he had the chance would he take  the serum lamar responds by saying  think of the amount of lives they could  have saved in afghanistan if they had it  between now and the time we see cap bend  a steel pipe it's implied he has taken  the serum and we'll later see him  tweaking out a possible side effect of  this  carly calls sarah and basically  threatens to kill her and her kids  unless she sets up a meeting between her  and sam  there's also a deep conversation about  how this new captain america means  nothing to her my world doesn't matter  to america so  why should i care about its mascot her  world meaning that of a black woman in  america  falcon in the winter soldier hasn't  shied away from politics  episode 2 delved into isaiah bradley and  its nod to the tuskegee experiments  this is also yet another hint that sam  her brother will  en