ntity  hidden with the power broker sam and  bucky and cal and lamar on her tail she  decides to separate them  and pick off captain america with their  eight hours up  io and two of her dora melanche nombel  and yama comfort zemo cap and lamar  arrive and a fight ensues with zemo  making an el chapo escape a nod to how  mexican drug lord  el chapo guzman escaped his prison via  hidden passageway under his cell's  washroom bucky is  literally disarmed something he didn't  know could happen which leads me to  believe this might happen again in the  future  cap however gets the worst of it getting  his ass beaten so hard he says  thank you sir i have another oh not that  one they weren't even super soldier  and this has all been part of how the  writers have been building up his  character so he'd get to the point where  we'd believe he'd take this super  soldier serum  this started all the way back in episode  2 when he talks about the pressure of  being the new cap  and living up to expectations everybody  in the world expects me to be  something and i don't want to fail them  in a one-on-one with his bff cap asked  lamar if he had the chance would he take  the serum lamar responds by saying  think of the amount of lives they could  have saved in afghanistan if they had it  between now and the time we see cap bend  a steel pipe it's implied he has taken  the serum and we'll later see him  tweaking out a possible side effect of  this  carly calls sarah and basically  threatens to kill her and her kids  unless she sets up a meeting between her  and sam  there's also a deep conversation about  how this new captain america means  nothing to her my world doesn't matter  to america so  why should i care about its mascot her  world meaning that of a black woman in  america  falcon in the winter soldier hasn't  shied away from politics  episode 2 delved into isaiah bradley and  its nod to the tuskegee experiments  this is also yet another hint that sam  her brother will  end up taking the shield sam meets up  with carly and to his surprise  she asks him to join her they both want  the same thing they just have  different ways of going about it sharon  warns sam that kappas found them out and  a fight ensues with carly killing lamar  before making a run for it this is the  last straw for jon who tracks down nico  one of the flag smashers and  kills him in cold blood the title of  this episode the whole world is watching  has  two meanings here not only is the whole  world watching as the public records  this violent act but the phrase itself  started as an anti-vietnam  war slogan and has since been picked up  by movements like black lives matter the  shield is  literally covered in blood a metaphor  for carly's view of it being a symbol of  oppression but as sam stated in episode  1  symbols  are nothing without the women and men  that give them meaning this new cap has  made the shield a symbol of  injustice whereas the old cap one of  courage justice and hope spoilers for  those who haven't seen the promotional  material but we see jon here looking as  though he's lamenting what has just  happened  and we see bucky and sam back in  louisiana with the shield  it's not certain yet if this new captain  america is relieved of his duty and it  goes to sam  or if sam forcibly takes it back from  him after watching this murder whatever  happens next we'll just have to wait  until next week  to find out thanks for watching everyone  if you liked the video be sure to give  it a like  subscribe and share for more bad takes  you can follow me on twitter and  instagram  at thinkstoryyt until next time remember  daddy loves you very much


